aneurysm.stl: synthetic bifurcation aneurysm, generated by us (no patient data). Licence: CC0.

Source: a signed-distance model (parent artery r = 2.0 mm with a straight inlet and a 60-degree bend of radius 8 mm,
daughters r = 1.65 mm and r = 1.40 mm at +70 and -62 degrees, saccular dome r = 3.6 mm on the apex, smooth unions)
sampled at 0.12 mm, iso-surfaced with VTK marching cubes, the ends clipped by planes, then processed once offline with
vmtk 1.5.0 (VTK 9.2.6, conda-forge, throwaway env via `pixi exec --spec vmtk`, never part of the project):
  vmtksurfacesmoothing -method taubin -iterations 20 -passband 0.1
  vmtksurfaceremeshing -elementsizemode edgelength -edgelength 0.45
  vmtkcenterlines -seedselector profileidlist   (inlet -> both outlets)
  vmtkflowextensions -adaptivelength 1 -extensionratio 5 -extensionmode centerlinedirection -boundarypoints 36
  vmtksurfacecapper -method centerpoint
Units: mm. Binary STL; the 2-byte attribute of each triangle is 0 wall, 1 inlet cap, 2 and 3 outlet caps.
